zweck.body:
The purpose of the association is to give people access to capable information technology and to digital education — regardless of their financial means.

It pursues this purpose in particular through:

a) testing, repairing and passing on used devices so that they stay in use for as long as possible (circular economy);
b) repair, advisory and support services for hardware and software;
c) educational offerings for digital participation;
d) the development and free publication of open-source software and of research results as a publicly accessible good;
e) offerings that give people with restricted access to the labour market a meaningful occupation.

The association is charitable and neutral in both religious and political terms. It does not pursue commercial ends and does not seek profit.

Economic activity is permitted insofar as it serves the fulfilment of the purpose and remains subordinate to it. It is a means to the purpose and never an end in itself.

The activity of the association is directed at the general public and not merely at its members.

mittel.body:
To pursue its purpose, the association has at its disposal:

a) membership fees;
b) contributions, donations, legacies and inheritances;
c) grants from public authorities and from foundations;
d) income from purpose-related activities and services;
e) income from the association's assets.

Any surplus remains entirely with the association and is used exclusively for the purpose set out in Art. 2. Any distribution to members or third parties is excluded.

The assets of the association are dedicated exclusively and irrevocably to its purpose.

erloeschen.body:
Membership ends:

a) for natural persons upon death, for legal entities upon dissolution;
b) by written resignation at the end of a financial year, subject to one month's notice;
c) by exclusion.

The board may exclude a member who harms the purpose of the association or who fails to meet their obligations despite a reminder. The member concerned may refer the decision to the general assembly within 30 days.

Members who have resigned or been excluded have no claim to the assets of the association.

organe.body:
The bodies of the association are:

a) the general assembly;
b) the board;
c) the auditors, if any are appointed.

generalversammlung.body:
The general assembly is the supreme body of the association. It is convened once a year in ordinary session, stating the agenda and with at least 20 days' notice.

The following non-transferable powers are vested in it:

a) approval of the annual report and the annual accounts;
b) discharge of the board;
c) election and removal of the members of the board and of any auditors;
d) setting the membership fee;
e) resolutions on compensation paid to members of the bodies (Art. 12);
f) amendment of the statutes;
g) dissolution of the association.

Each member has one vote. Resolutions are passed by a simple majority of the votes cast; in the event of a tie, the chair casts the deciding vote.

An extraordinary general assembly is convened by resolution of the board or at the written request of at least one fifth of the members.

Resolutions may also be passed in writing or electronically, provided that no member requests an oral deliberation.
